\deflang1033\pard\plain\f2\fs24\b\ul Please Read Me!
\par \plain\f2\fs24 
\par This file serves as the user's manual for the Universal Media Player (UMP). UMP is a simple program, similiar to your Audio CD player program or desk accessory. It gives you easy access to all the enhanced features and content on this CD.
\par 
\par \plain\f2\fs24\b\ul This document is generic. It applies to all discs using Universal Media Player, not specifically this one.
\par \plain\f2\fs24 
\par If you are an experienced computer enthusiast, you can just experiment with the UMP and figure it out pretty quickly, but for best results we suggest you read the stuff below.
\par 
\par Suggested minimum system: You need a Windows-95 computer with a Pentium processor or better, at least 8 megabytes of RAM, a double-speed CD-ROM drive (or better), color monitor capable of displaying thousands of colors, a Windows-95 compatible sound card and stereo speakers.
\par 
\par You need a few other things to use this disc.
\par 
\par 1) UMP. (You probably have it installed already, or are in the process of installing it right now.)
\par 
\par 2) An account with an Internet Service Provider (ISP) or online service, and a functioning Email program and World Wide Web browser (or both functions in one program).
\par 
\par \plain\f2\fs24\cf0 3) If there are videos on this disc you will need Apple's \plain\f2\fs24\cf0\b Quicktime \plain\f2\fs24\cf0 software. (They will appear by name in the "Video" menu, under the filmstrip icon). If there are videos on the disc and you don't yet have it, you can install Quicktime 3 \plain\f2\fs24\cf0\b\ul and\plain\f2\fs24\cf0  Quicktime 2.1.2 from this disc. Just click the \plain\f2\fs24\cf0\b Install Quicktime\plain\f2\fs24\cf0  button in UMP's prefs dialog box.. The installer will automatically give you BOTH versions (3.0.1 and 2.1.2). The two versions can co-exist harmlessly on one computer. The older version is required for compatibility with a lot of older multimedia software.
\par \plain\f2\fs24 
\par \plain\f2\fs24\b Installation:
\par \plain\f2\fs24 
\par The first time you insert this disc, the installer for the Universal Media Player will automatically run. It will also run if you have an older version of UMP installed, in order to give you the new one. It's a very fast, simple installation, and UMP will be available in the Windows-95 Start->Programs menu once its complete. UMP will start running automatically every time you insert an UMP-compatible Enhanced CD into the drive.
\par 
\par \plain\f2\fs24\b How to use UMP:
\par \plain\f2\fs24 
\par UMP will start up with a small window, with five buttons across the top, and a small album graphic. (To see the pictures on the disc, click the "Maximize" button on the (top) menu bar of the UMP window).
\par 
\par The buttons look like this, and here's what they do:
